      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:50:2",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الصَّلَاةِ خَلْفَ الْمُخَالِفِينَ فَقَالَ مَا هُمْ عِنْدِي إِلَّا بِمَنْزِلَةِ الْجُدُرِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "From him, from Ahmad, from Abdullah Bin Muhammad Al Hajjal, from Sa’alba, from Zurara who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> about the <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> behind the adversaries. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘They are not in my<sup>asws</sup> presence except at the status of the walls (bunch of bricks)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. It is a narration from him (narrator of previous Hadith) by Ahmad from ‘Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Hajjal from Tha’labah from Zurarah who has said the following: “I once asked abu Ja’far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about performing Salah (prayer) behind those who oppose our belief. He (the Imam) said, ‘To me they are but walls (scarecrows).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
